# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# Coverage profiles from `cargo llvm-cov`. Most land under target/, but a test
# that spawns a subprocess with a cleared environment loses LLVM_PROFILE_FILE,
# and the child then falls back to LLVM's default name and drops it in whatever
# directory it was started from.
*.profraw

# Nothing about spikes/ is listed here on purpose. Every spike is committed, and
# each one ignores its own build output in its own .gitignore — the knowledge of
# what a stack generates belongs next to the stack that generates it. A blanket
# `spikes/*` with negations used to live here, and its failure mode was that a
# new file in spikes/ was invisible until somebody remembered to add an
# exception for it.

# The `jose` verification harness. Node verifies tokens; it never builds them.
scripts/node_modules/
scripts/package-lock.json

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
